{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; require \\\"json\\\"; require \\\"json-schema\\\"; schema=JSON.parse(File.read(\\\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\\\")); data=YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.yaml\\\"); JSON::Validator.validate\"'!(schema, data); puts \"hypothesis schema: valid\"'\"' 2>&1 || (sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.yaml; exit 1)\ngit diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.yaml\ngit status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r1s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"/System/Library/Frameworks/Ruby.framework/Versions/2.6/usr/lib/ruby/2.6.0/rubygems/core_ext/kernel_require.rb:54:in `require': cannot load such file -- json-schema (LoadError)\n\tfrom /System/Library/Frameworks/Ruby.framework/Versions/2.6/usr/lib/ruby/2.6.0/rubygems/core_ext/kernel_require.rb:54:in `require'\n\tfrom -e:1:in `<main>'\nid: hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\ntitle: \"Iterative RV32M divide unit\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The routed Fmax critical path is the combinational divide/remainder network\n  from the ID/EX register into the EX/MEM register. It is a long LUT-and-mux\n  chain, while the CoreMark timed loop executes after the setup-time DIVU\n  instructions, so replacing it need not reduce measured IPC.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the inferred combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators with a\n  small restoring iterative divider. On a divide or remainder instruction,\n  EX will issue the operands into the unit, drain older pipeline work, hold\n  the frontend until completion, then inject one normal EX/MEM result. Keep\n  all RV32M corner cases exact and retain the ALTOPS behavior for formal.\n  This removes the measured critical combinational path while confining the\n  multi-cycle penalty to the rare non-timed divide operations.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove real combinational divide/remainder operators from the Fmax path while preserving the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS cases.\"\n  - file: rtl/divider.sv\n    description: \"Add a sequential unsigned restoring divider with signed pre/post-processing and architecturally defined zero and overflow cases.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Issue DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU to the divider, hold their pipeline payload until completion, and inject the returned result once.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a divide-in-flight interlock that preserves program order without duplicate retirement or writeback.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the divide interlock and result path between execute, hazard control, and the new divider.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Extend RV32M coverage for iterative DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU latency and all specified corner cases.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
