{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r3s0.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r3s0.yaml && rg -n 'hypothesis\\\\.schema|jsonschema|validate.*hypoth' tools Makefile .github 2>/dev/null\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Shared sign-configurable multiplier\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The ALU currently evaluates signed-signed, unsigned-unsigned, and\n  signed-unsigned 64-bit products on every cycle, then selects one product\n  for an RV32M multiply instruction. These parallel arithmetic cones consume\n  LUTs and routing even though only one product can retire per instruction.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the three unconditional multiplier expressions with one 33-by-33\n  signed multiplier whose operand extensions are selected from the ALU op:\n  signed/signed for MULH, zero/zero for MULHU, and signed/zero for MULHSU.\n  MUL reads the shared product low word, which is identical for every signed\n  interpretation. This preserves one-cycle exact RV32M multiply semantics and\n  the formal ALTOPS branch, while reducing arithmetic duplication and routing\n  pressure enough to improve Tang Nano placement and Fmax without adding a\n  stall or touching fetch prediction.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Replace three unconditional RV32M product datapaths with one sign-configurable 33-bit multiplier and select its architecturally correct low or high word.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Add directed and randomized boundary vectors spanning MUL, MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU to prove the shared sign-extension mapping.\"\ntools/tournament.py:218:    import jsonschema\ntools/tournament.py:220:        emit_verilog, offlimits_changes, _read_notes, validate_hypothesis,\ntools/tournament.py:261:        hyp = validate_hypothesis(hyp_path)\ntools/tournament.py:262:    except (jsonschema.ValidationError, FileNotFoundError, yaml.YAMLError) as e:\ntools/agents/hypothesis.py:282:## Required YAML structure (validates against schemas/hypothesis.schema.json)\ntools/orchestrator.py:6:import jsonschema, yaml\ntools/orchestrator.py:48:HYP_SCHEMA     = json.loads(Path(\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\").read_text())\ntools/orchestrator.py:444:def validate_hypothesis(hyp_path: str) -> dict:\ntools/orchestrator.py:447:    jsonschema.validate(hyp, HYP_SCHEMA)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
