 DSP-attributed 17-by-17 limb multipliers, signedness-selected high limbs, and a width-safe recombination tree; retain real DIV/REM and ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add adversarial and randomized MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU vectors across limb carry boundaries and every signedness combination to prove the tiled product is bit exact.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Decompose the shared exact signed 33-bit product into four DSP-attributed 17-by-17 limb multipliers, signedness-selected high limbs, and a width-safe recombination tree; retain real DIV/REM and ALTOPS behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Add adversarial and randomized MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU vectors across limb carry boundaries and every signedness combination to prove the tiled product is bit exact.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 339.14, \"delta_pct\": -7.25, \"vs_baseline\": 19.91, \"fmax_mhz\": 137.12, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4043217, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10678, \"ff\": 1922, \"seeds\": [137.12, 141.92, 128.37], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:13:51.983420Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-001-r6s0 (regression, -7.25%): On the Tang Nano RV32M datapath, splitting the shared 33-bit multiplier into four DSP-forced 17-by-17 signed partial products regresses because the widened signed partial-product recombination and extra multiplier placement/routing outweigh the benefit of smaller inferred multipliers.\"}\n18:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"Narrow execution and trace pipes\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX/MEM and MEM/WB bundles carry every RVFI-only source value,\\nPC field, branch field, and memory-observation field beside the live\\nexecute datapath. Those wide bundled registers and their broad module\\ninterfaces increase routing pressure around the ALU, forwarding muxes, and\\nmemory stage even though most fields do not affect forward progress.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX/MEM and MEM/WB bundles carry every RVFI-only source value,\\nPC field, branch field, and memory-observation field beside the live\\nexecute datapath. Those wide bundled registers and their broad module\\ninterfaces increase routing pressure around the ALU, forwarding muxes, and\\nmemory stage even though most fields do not affect forward progress.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Partition the pipeline into a narrow execution pipe and a lockstep\\nretirement-trace pipe. The execution pipe keeps only data and control that\\nthe following stage consumes for architectural execution, while a sideband\\ntrace record carries RVFI-only operand, PC, instruction, and memory\\nobservations to the same single retirement boundary. Both pipes use the\\nidentical valid/hold/flush enables, so retirement order and every RVFI\\nvalue remain unchanged. Reducing wide high-fanout execute-stage bundles\\nshould improve Tang Nano placement and Fmax without adding an IPC penalty.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the existing EX/MEM and MEM/WB payload definitions into compact execution records and lockstep RVFI trace records, keeping all architectural fields represented exactly once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Register only live ALU, store-data, destination, control, and valid state on the execution path while emitting a separately registered trace record containing post-forward source observations and resolved PC metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrow execution record for the memory transaction, update the trace r