t_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add equivalence-oriented pipeline cases covering ALU, load, store, branch, redirect, and random bus stalls, checking unchanged RVFI operands, memory fields, order, and single retirement.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 352.96, \"delta_pct\": -3.47, \"vs_baseline\": 24.8, \"fmax_mhz\": 142.71, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4043217, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10324, \"ff\": 1922, \"seeds\": [148.3, 141.7, 142.71], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:16:23.649583Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-002-r6s1 (regression, -3.47%): Splitting EX/MEM and MEM/WB into lockstep execution and RVFI-trace records does not remove the trace state or its routing, so the added parallel interfaces and control can outweigh localized datapath narrowing on Tang Nano.\"}\n19:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Shared static predictor target adder\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current successful static predictor forms PC+4, PC+JAL-immediate,\\nand PC+branch-immediate in parallel before selecting one result. Those\\nredundant 32-bit adders and their routing sit in the fetch next-PC cone,\\ndespite only one successor ever being required each cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current successful static predictor forms PC+4, PC+JAL-immediate,\\nand PC+branch-immediate in parallel before selecting one result. Those\\nredundant 32-bit adders and their routing sit in the fetch next-PC cone,\\ndespite only one successor ever being required each cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Preserve the current direct-JAL and opcode-biased backward BNE/BLT/BLTU\\nprediction policy, but first select a single predicted displacement\\n(four, JAL immediate, or branch immediate) and then compute the successor\\nwith one shared PC adder. This retains identical predicted PCs, EX