ned multiplier\tregression\t339.14\t-7.25\nhyp-20260710-002-r6s1\tstructural\tNarrow execution and trace pipes\tregression\t352.96\t-3.47\nhyp-20260710-003-r6s2\tpredictor\tShared static predictor target adder\tregression\t337.65\t-7.66\nhyp-20260710-001-r7s0\tmicro_opt\tShared EX branch comparison primitives\tregression\t319.47\t-12.63\nhyp-20260710-002-r7s1\tstructural\tResetless valid-tag register file\tregression\t317.99\t-13.03\nhyp-20260710-003-r7s2\tpredictor\tMinimized static loop predictor\tregression\t284.58\t-22.17\n5-{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Zero-bubble load-use forwarding\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The present five-stage pipeline always injects one bubble between a load\\nand its immediate consumer. CoreMark makes frequent pointer and array\\naccesses, so this conservative interlock reduces useful issue bandwidth.\\nThe target memory interface returns read data combinationally on accepted\\nzero-wait cycles, making a late MEM-to-EX bypass possible without changing\\nthe architectural bus contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The present five-stage pipeline always injects one bubble between a load\\nand its immediate consumer. CoreMark makes frequent pointer and array\\naccesses, so this conservative interlock reduces useful issue bandwidth.\\nThe target memory interface returns read data combinationally on accepted\\nzero-wait cycles, making a late MEM-to-EX bypass possible without changing\\nthe architectural bus contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a dedicated MEM-load-to-EX forwarding path carrying the load result\\nafter its byte-lane extraction and sign/zero extension. When EX/MEM holds\\na valid, aligned load and dmemReady is high, an immediately dependent\\ninstruction in EX selects that result instead of the load address, so the\\nload-use interlock no longer injects its otherwise mandatory bubble. Keep\\nthe pair frozen under dmem backpressure and suppress the bypass for\\nmisaligned trapping accesses; therefore retirement order, RVFI operand\\nvalues, and all existing exception behavior remain unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the existing extracted load result plus a valid signal qualified by a real, aligned accepted load for same-cycle bypassing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Distinguish an EX/MEM load from an ALU producer and select the dedicated MEM-load forwarding source for matching EX operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the MEM-load forwarding input and select it for either source operand while retaining ALU and WB forwarding priority rules.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the proactive load-use bubble; retain the full-pipeline hold for an unaccepted dmem transaction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the qualified load-result bypass from MEM to execute and the revised forwarding controls without changing core IO or RVFI retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Replace the one-bubble load-use expectation with directed zero-wait and dmem-stalled dependency tests that check data, RVFI order, and single retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the existing extracted load result plus a valid signal qualified by a real, aligned accepted load for same-cycle bypassing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Distinguish an EX/MEM load from an ALU producer and select the dedicated MEM-load forwarding source for matching EX operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the MEM-load forwarding input and select it for either source operand while retaining ALU and WB forwarding priority rules.\"}, {\"file\"