{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'dsp|mul|divider|critical|timing|fmax|frequency|clock' cores/bench/experiments cores/bench/fpga fpga Makefile 2>/dev/null | head -n 240 && rg --files cores/bench | rg '(report|json|log|tcl|ys|sv)\"'$'\"' | head -n 160\"","aggregated_output":"Makefile:48:# Multi-core: TARGET selects the core under cores/<TARGET>/.\nMakefile:82:\t@echo \"  make fpga TARGET=v1     — FPGA fitness eval (Fmax + CoreMark cycles)\"\nMakefile:94:# -Wno-MULTITOP: until phase 2's core.sv lands and instantiates everything,\nMakefile:95:# rtl/ legitimately has multiple top modules. Drop this once phase 2 is in.\nMakefile:98:\t  verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+$(RTL_DIR) \\\nMakefile:124:# evaluates the actual MUL/DIV/REM bitvector formulas. SLOW (each\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-d2637a0\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T00:54:39.837121Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Iterative RV32M divide unit\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The routed Fmax critical path is the combinational divide/remainder network\\nfrom the ID/EX register into the EX/MEM register. It is a long LUT-and-mux\\nchain, while the CoreMark timed loop executes after the setup-time DIVU\\ninstructions, so replacing it need not reduce measured IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The routed Fmax critical path is the combinational divide/remainder network\\nfrom the ID/EX register into the EX/MEM register. It is a long LUT-and-mux\\nchain, while the CoreMark timed loop executes after the setup-time DIVU\\ninstructions, so replacing it need not reduce measured IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the inferred combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators with a\\nsmall restoring iterative divider. On a divide or remainder instruction,\\nEX will issue the operands into the unit, drain older pipeline work, hold\\nthe frontend until completion, then inject one normal EX/MEM result. Keep\\nall RV32M corner cases exact and retain the ALTOPS behavior for formal.\\nThis removes the measured critical combinational path while confining the\\nmulti-cycle penalty to the rare non-timed divide operations.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 10, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide/remainder operators from the Fmax path while preserving the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a sequential unsigned restoring divider with signed pre/post-processing and architecturally defined zero and overflow cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Issue DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU to the divider, hold their pipeline payload until completion, and inject the returned result once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a divide-in-flight interlock that preserves program order without duplicate retirement or writeback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divide interlock and result path between execute, hazard control, and the new divider.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend RV32M coverage for iterative DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU latency and all specified corner cases.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 10, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide/remainder operators from the Fmax path while preserving the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a sequential unsigned restoring divider with signed pre/post-processing and architecturally defined zero and overflow cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Issue DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU to the divider, hold their pipeline payload until completion, and inject the returned result once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a divide-in-flight interlock that preserves program order without duplicate retirement or writeback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divide interlock and result path between execute, hazard control, and the new divider.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend RV32M coverage for iterative DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU latency and all specified corner cases.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 1}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Iterative divider execution unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The ALU unconditionally elaborates signed and unsigned divide and remainder\\ndatapaths, although CoreMark's timed kernels are dominated by loads, integer\\nALU operations, branches, and multiply-accumulate work. Four combinational\\ndivision/modulo expressions consume scarce LUT fabric and can set the slowest\\nALU route, limiting Fmax to 127 MHz near the LUT budget.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The ALU unconditionally elaborates signed and unsigned divide and remainder\\ndatapaths, although CoreMark's timed kernels are dominated by loads, integer\\nALU operations, branches, and multiply-accumulate work. Four combinational\\ndivision/modulo expressions consume scarce LUT fabric and can set the slowest\\nALU route, limiting Fmax to 127 MHz near the LUT budget.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU implementation with one shared\\n32-cycle restoring divider that stalls the in-order execute path only for an\\nM divide/remainder instruction. Preserve the existing single-cycle path for\\nall other ALU and multiply operations. The rare divide latency should be\\noutside, or negligible within, the timed CoreMark kernel, while removing the\\nwide combinational divider should improve placement headroom and Fmax enough\\nto raise Fmax times CoreMark IPC.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the synthesised combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapaths while retaining the real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS semantics for non-divide ALU operations.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a shared signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with request, busy, completion, quotient, and remainder interfaces, including all RV32M divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 corner cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact control metadata identifying the four divide/remainder ALU operations for execute-stage dispatch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Turn EX into a small execute sequencer: launch divider operations once, hold the instruction and redirect state while busy, and emit the completed quotient or remainder exactly once into EX/MEM.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an execute-busy interlock that freezes younger IF/ID and ID/EX work without duplicating retirements or losing redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire divider-busy control into the pipeline stall policy while preserving the existing RVFI retirement boundary and nret=1 IO contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Keep exact RV32M division and remainder edge-case coverage against the new functional-unit result path.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed DIV/REM dependency and bus-stall tests to verify a single retirement, correct forwarding, and progress through the multi-cycle EX hold.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the synthesised combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU datapaths while retaining the real and RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS semantics for non-divide ALU operations.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a shared signed/unsigned iterative restoring divider with request, busy, completion, quotient, and remainder interfaces, including all RV32M divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 corner cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact control metadata identifying the four divide/remainder ALU operations for execute-stage dispatch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Turn EX into a small execute sequencer: launch divider operations once, hold the instruction and redirect state while busy, and emit the completed quotient or remainder exactly once into EX/MEM.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an execute-busy interlock that freezes younger IF/ID and ID/EX work without duplicating retirements or losing redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire divider-busy control into the pipeline stall policy while preserving the existing RVFI retirement boundary and nret=1 IO contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Keep exact RV32M division and remainder edge-case coverage against the new functional-unit result path.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed DIV/REM dependency and bus-stall tests to verify a single retirement, correct forwarding, and progress through the multi-cycle EX hold.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"cosim_failed: selftest.elf\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static loop branch prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The five-stage core always fetches PC+4 until EX resolves a branch or\\njump, so every taken loop back-edge discards useful fetch/decode work.\\nCoreMark contains many short counted loops, making this recurring control\\nhazard a material IPC limiter even with the zero-wait FPGA instruction bus.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The five-stage core always fetches PC+4 until EX resolves a branch or\\njump, so every taken loop back-edge discards useful fetch/decode work.\\nCoreMark contains many short counted loops, making this recurring control\\nhazard a material IPC limiter even with the zero-wait FPGA instruction bus.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a combinational static BTFNT predictor in IF: predict direct JALs and\\nbackward conditional branches taken, using their encoded PC-relative\\nimmediate, and otherwise predict fall-through. Carry the prediction with\\nthe instruction and have EX redirect and flush only on a misprediction;\\nJALR remains fall-through predicted. Correct loop-back predictions admit\\nthe target instruction into decode instead of paying the current recovery\\nbubble, while avoiding the LUT and timing cost of a BTB or dynamic table.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode direct control-flow immediates at fetch, select static BTFNT/JAL next PC, and accept EX recovery only for mispredictions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend IF/ID and ID/EX payloads with prediction metadata needed to validate speculative fetch in EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch IF prediction metadata beside the decoded instruction into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare predicted and resolved next PCs, producing a recovery redirect and flush only for control-flow mispredictions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire prediction metadata and misprediction recovery through the pipeline and hazard control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace unconditional EX-control-flow flushing with misprediction-only flushing while retaining load and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed BTFNT, direct-JAL, fall-through, and misprediction-recovery tests including RVFI PC sequencing.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Decode direct control-flow immediates at fetch, select static BTFNT/JAL next PC, and accept EX recovery only for mispredictions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Extend IF/ID and ID/EX payloads with prediction metadata needed to validate speculative fetch in EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Latch IF prediction metadata beside the decoded instruction into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare predicted and resolved next PCs, producing a recovery redirect and flush only for control-flow mispredictions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire prediction metadata and misprediction recovery through the pipeline and hazard control.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace unconditional EX-control-flow flushing with misprediction-only flushing while retaining load and bus-stall priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed BTFNT, direct-JAL, fall-through, and misprediction-recovery tests including RVFI PC sequencing.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 310.0, \"delta_pct\": 9.61, \"vs_baseline\": 9.61, \"fmax_mhz\": 132.05, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4259699, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10490, \"ff\": 1896, \"seeds\": [132.05, 135.98, 130.96], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:03:04.687018Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (improvement, +9.61%): Carrying IF's predicted next PC to EX lets a static BTFNT policy avoid recovery bubbles on CoreMark's frequent backward counted-loop branches (and direct JALs), making low-cost fetch-side control prediction an effective IPC optimization without a BTB.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:5:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Zero-bubble load-use forwarding\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The present five-stage pipeline always injects one bubble between a load\\nand its immediate consumer. CoreMark makes frequent pointer and array\\naccesses, so this conservative interlock reduces useful issue bandwidth.\\nThe target memory interface returns read data combinationally on accepted\\nzero-wait cycles, making a late MEM-to-EX bypass possible without changing\\nthe architectural bus contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The present five-stage pipeline always injects one bubble between a load\\nand its immediate consumer. CoreMark makes frequent pointer and array\\naccesses, so this conservative interlock reduces useful issue bandwidth.\\nThe target memory interface returns read data combinationally on accepted\\nzero-wait cycles, making a late MEM-to-EX bypass possible without changing\\nthe architectural bus contract.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a dedicated MEM-load-to-EX forwarding path carrying the load result\\nafter its byte-lane extraction and sign/zero extension. When EX/MEM holds\\na valid, aligned load and dmemReady is high, an immediately dependent\\ninstruction in EX selects that result instead of the load address, so the\\nload-use interlock no longer injects its otherwise mandatory bubble. Keep\\nthe pair frozen under dmem backpressure and suppress the bypass for\\nmisaligned trapping accesses; therefore retirement order, RVFI operand\\nvalues, and all existing exception behavior remain unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the existing extracted load result plus a valid signal qualified by a real, aligned accepted load for same-cycle bypassing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Distinguish an EX/MEM load from an ALU producer and select the dedicated MEM-load forwarding source for matching EX operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the MEM-load forwarding input and select it for either source operand while retaining ALU and WB forwarding priority rules.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the proactive load-use bubble; retain the full-pipeline hold for an unaccepted dmem transaction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the qualified load-result bypass from MEM to execute and the revised forwarding controls without changing core IO or RVFI retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Replace the one-bubble load-use expectation with directed zero-wait and dmem-stalled dependency tests that check data, RVFI order, and single retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the existing extracted load result plus a valid signal qualified by a real, aligned accepted load for same-cycle bypassing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Distinguish an EX/MEM load from an ALU producer and select the dedicated MEM-load forwarding source for matching EX operands.\"}, {\"file\"