{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; x=YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r9s0.yaml\\\"); abort(\\\"wrong id\\\") unless x[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20260710-001-r9s0\\\"; abort(\\\"wrong category\\\") unless x[\\\"category\\\"] == \\\"micro_opt\\\"; abort(\\\"bad impact\\\") unless x.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\").is_a?(Integer) && x.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"confidence\\\") == \\\"medium\\\"; abort(\\\"bad paths\\\") unless x[\\\"changes\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(%r{\\\\A(?:rtl/|test/test_).*}) }; puts \\\"YAML structure verified: #{x[\\\"changes\\\"].length} changes\\\"' && git diff --check -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r9s0.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-001-r9s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"YAML structure verified: 6 changes\nid: hyp-20260710-001-r9s0\ntitle: \"Fine-grained base ALU partition\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The class-partitioned ALU control raised fitness by keeping ordinary RV32I\n  execution out of the RV32M result mux, but the base-class path still selects\n  among ADD/SUB, logic, compare, shift, and LUI results with one four-bit\n  opcode. CoreMark's hot address-generation and integer-update operations are\n  overwhelmingly ADD-class, so that remaining broad base selection is a likely\n  control-to-EX routing and mux cost on the Tang Nano.\nhypothesis: |\n  Refine only the base ALU encoding into a coarse result class plus a local\n  sub-operation. Give ADD/SUB and AUIPC address-generation a dedicated class\n  so their output is selected before the logic, compare, shift, and LUI cones;\n  the local sub-operation is consumed only inside its selected class. Retain\n  the existing RV32M class split, all ALU results, forwarding, and single-cycle\n  latency. This extends the proven class-first mux partitioning to the common\n  RV32I path, aiming to shorten its registered-control-to-ALU-result cone\n  without adding frontend state or changing CoreMark IPC.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Replace the flat base ALU operation encoding with compact base result-class and class-local sub-operation fields while retaining the RV32M class encoding.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Emit the refined base result class only in validated opcode and funct matches, preserving the default-illegal discipline.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Carry the refined base ALU control through the ID/EX payload without changing valid, flush, or operand capture behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Connect the refined base ALU control to execute while preserving forwarding, branch resolution, and EX/MEM timing.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Split the base result mux by coarse ADD, logic, compare, shift, and pass-through classes, with sub-operation selection local to each class and unchanged RV32M handling.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Add control-class boundary vectors covering every RV32I base result class, AUIPC/LUI routing, shifts, comparisons, and RV32M non-regression.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
