{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; require \\\"json\\\"; p YAML.load_file(ARGV[0])' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml && git status --short cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r2s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\"=>\"hyp-20260710-002-r2s1\", \"title\"=>\"MEM-to-EX load forwarding\", \"category\"=>\"structural\", \"motivation\"=>\"The current five-stage pipeline inserts a full bubble for every immediate\\nload consumer, even when the zero-wait data-memory response is already\\navailable combinationally during the load's MEM stage. CoreMark has many\\npointer-chasing and state-update sequences where this fixed interlock\\nreduces useful issue bandwidth.\\n\", \"hypothesis\"=>\"Add a late MEM-to-EX bypass that forwards a load's fully extracted and\\nsign/zero-extended dmem result directly to the following instruction's EX\\noperand mux. Remove the normal load-use bubble; when io_dmemReady is low,\\nretain the existing whole-pipeline memory hold so no consumer observes an\\nunacknowledged load. This converts adjacent load-consumer pairs from two\\nexecution cycles to one in the common zero-wait case while preserving\\nin-order retirement, RVFI source values, and precise bus-stall behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\"=>{\"fitness_delta_pct\"=>6, \"confidence\"=>\"medium\"}, \"changes\"=>[{\"file\"=>\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Expose the combinationally extracted, sign/zero-extended load value as a dedicated forwarding result alongside the existing MEM/WB capture path.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Distinguish an EX/MEM load from an ALU producer so the youngest matching source selects the late load-data bypass rather than its address result.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Add the MEM-stage load-data input to the EX operand muxes and use it for immediately dependent ALU, store-data, branch, and JALR operands.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Remove the fixed load-use bubble while retaining dmem-ready holds, redirect recovery, and all other pipeline interlocks.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\"=>\"Wire the MEM load-result bypass and load classification through the forwarding network without changing the nret=1 top-level contract.\"}, {\"file\"=>\"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\"=>\"Add adjacent load-to-ALU, load-to-store, load-to-branch, and random dmem-backpressure tests covering forwarding, stalls, and one retirement per instruction.\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
