{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1.yaml && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260710-002-r3s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260710-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"Ordered single-entry store buffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Random dmem backpressure currently freezes every pipeline stage whenever a\n  store reaches MEM, even though its address, data, and byte enables are\n  already known. CoreMark has regular state and array stores, so these waits\n  unnecessarily prevent independent ALU work and fetch from progressing.\nhypothesis: |\n  Insert a one-entry ordered store buffer between MEM and dmem. A normal RAM\n  store can leave the pipeline once captured in the buffer, while the buffer\n  retries its bus transaction until io_dmemReady accepts it; a following load\n  waits for the buffer to drain, preserving RV32 memory order without a\n  complex merge path. MMIO stores remain synchronous and drain prior buffered\n  work before issue, preserving UART and timing-marker ordering. This removes\n  full-pipeline stalls for store-only backpressure while retaining precise\n  load behavior, RVFI retirement order, and the existing external interface.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/store_buffer.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry valid/ready store queue that retains aligned address, replicated write data, and byte mask until an acknowledged dmem write.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Classify normal RAM versus strongly ordered MMIO stores, enqueue eligible stores without waiting for dmemReady, and keep loads ordered behind an occupied buffer.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace unconditional store dmem holds with load/MMIO ordering stalls and buffer-full backpressure while retaining all existing redirect priorities.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the store buffer onto the unchanged dmem ports and connect occupancy, drain, and acceptance signals to MEM and hazard control.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add any compact pipeline metadata needed to distinguish buffered stores from loads and strongly ordered MMIO accesses.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add random dmem-stalled store streams, store-to-load ordering, partial-byte stores, UART/MMIO marker ordering, and RVFI single-retirement checks.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
