LR, so that fixed extra\\nstage costs IPC. The failed RAS attempt shows this benefit should not be\\nbought with more target-selection logic on the fetch critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Resolve dependency-free, aligned legal JALRs in ID using the existing\\nwrite-first regfile value and redirect fetch at the ID/EX boundary. Record\\nthe resolved target as that instruction's predicted successor so its normal\\nEX pass does not redirect again. If the immediately older EX instruction\\nwrites JALR's rs1, or the target is misaligned, defer to the present EX\\nresolver and trap path. EX redirects retain priority over an ID redirect,\\nensuring a wrong-path JALR is flushed. This removes one recovery cycle for\\nordinary returns without widening the IF prediction datapath or changing\\nretirement order.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize accepted dependency-free JALRs, compute their aligned rs1-plus-immediate target, emit an early redirect, and carry that target as pred_next_pc while retaining EX fallback cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Distinguish older EX recovery from an ID JALR redirect: flush IF for either source, but flush ID only for the older EX redirect so the redirecting JALR still advances once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Arbitrate EX-over-ID redirects, gate early JALR recovery on the absence of an immediately older rs1 producer and memory holds, and preserve the single-channel RVFI boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept the arbitrated earlier redirect with the existing redirect-over-stall priority, emitting a bubble for the speculative fetch slot.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain the existing resolved-versus-predicted comparison so deferred or dependency-bound JALRs recover in EX and early-resolved JALRs cannot redirect twice.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add return-style JALR, ALU-to-JALR dependency fallback, load-to-JALR under dmem backpressure, misaligned-target trap, and simultaneous older-redirect tests with RVFI PC and order checks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Recognize accepted dependency-free JALRs, compute their aligned rs1-plus-immediate target, emit an early redirect, and carry that target as pred_next_pc while retaining EX fallback cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Distinguish older EX recovery from an ID JALR redirect: flush IF for either source, but flush ID only for the older EX redirect so the redirecting JALR still advances once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Arbitrate EX-over-ID redirects, gate early JALR recovery on the absence of an immediately older rs1 producer and memory holds, and preserve the single-channel RVFI boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept the arbitrated earlier redirect with the existing redirect-over-stall priority, emitting a bubble for the speculative fetch slot.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retain the existing resolved-versus-predicted comparison so deferred or dependency-bound JALRs recover in EX and early-resolved JALRs cannot redirect twice.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add return-style JALR, ALU-to-JALR dependency fallback, load-to-JALR under dmem backpressure, misaligned-target trap, and simultaneous older-redirect tests with RVFI PC and order checks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 324.04, \"delta_pct\": -10.37, \"vs_baseline\": 14.57, \"fmax_mhz\": 130.96, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4041507, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10369, \"ff\": 1923, \"seeds\": [132.22, 130.96, 126.37], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed