 — without\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:66:  // this priority the redirect target would be silently dropped, the\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:72:    else if (redirect) pc <= redirect_target;\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:80:    out.instr = (flush || redirect) ? 32'h0000_0013 : imem_data;\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:81:    out.pred_next_pc = (flush || redirect) ? (pc + 32'd4)\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:82:                                             : predicted_next_pc;\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv:83:    out.valid = !(flush || redirect);\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:3:// Handles redirects and bus backpressure.  Load-use dependencies do not\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:12://   flush_if / flush_id : on EX misprediction recovery, kill the in-flight\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:14://   flush_id            : kills ID's own register on redirect recovery.\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:19:  input  logic       redirect,          // EX has detected a misprediction\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:50:    // instruction this cycle (redirect target unknown to IF, or imem\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:52:    flush_if      = redirect || imem_stall;\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:55:    //   - redirect    -> bubble      (kill wrong-path)\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:57:    // dmem_stall takes precedence over redirect's bubble so the in-flight\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv:61:    flush_id      = redirect && !dmem_stall;\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:4:// MEM/WB), runs the ALU, resolves branches, computes the redirect\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:5:// target.  The predicted successor from IF is compared with the resolved\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:6:// successor, so recovery and flushing occur only on a misprediction. Owns\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:29:  output logic               redirect,\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:30:  output logic [31:0]        redirect_target\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:98:  // instruction, suppress the redirect (PC stays linear), and c