imed loop executes after the setup-time DIVU\\ninstructions, so replacing it need not reduce measured IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The routed Fmax critical path is the combinational divide/remainder network\\nfrom the ID/EX register into the EX/MEM register. It is a long LUT-and-mux\\nchain, while the CoreMark timed loop executes after the setup-time DIVU\\ninstructions, so replacing it need not reduce measured IPC.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the inferred combinational DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators with a\\nsmall restoring iterative divider. On a divide or remainder instruction,\\nEX will issue the operands into the unit, drain older pipeline work, hold\\nthe frontend until completion, then inject one normal EX/MEM result. Keep\\nall RV32M corner cases exact and retain the ALTOPS behavior for formal.\\nThis removes the measured critical combinational path while confining the\\nmulti-cycle penalty to the rare non-timed divide operations.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 10, \"confidence\": \"high\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real combinational divide/remainder operators from the Fmax path while preserving the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divider.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a sequential unsigned restoring divider with signed pre/post-processing and architecturally defined zero and overflow cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Issue DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU to the divider, hold their pipeline payload until completion, and inject the returned result once.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a divide-in-flight interlock that preserves program order without duplicate retirement or writeback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the divide interlock and result path between execute, hazard control, and the new divider.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_alu.py\", \"description\": \"Extend RV32M coverage for iterative DIV/