{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"node -e 'const fs=require(\\\"fs\\\");for(const l of fs.readFileSync(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\",\\\"utf8\\\").trim().split(\\\"\\\\n\\\")){const x=JSON.parse(l);if(x.category===\\\"predictor\\\") console.log(JSON.stringify({id:x.id,title:x.title,outcome:x.outcome,fitness:x.fitness,delta_pct:x.delta_pct,fmax_mhz:x.fmax_mhz,cycles:x.cycles,hypothesis:(x.hypothesis&&x.hypothesis.hypothesis)||x.hypothesis,changes:x.changes},null,2))}'\nprintf '\\\\n--- hypothesis schema relevant constraints ---\\\\n'\nsed -n '1,220p' schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\nprintf '\\\\n--- target status ---\\\\n'\ngit status --short\nls -ld cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r1s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Static loop branch prediction\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 310,\n  \"delta_pct\": 9.61,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 132.05,\n  \"cycles\": 4259699,\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Add a combinational static BTFNT predictor in IF: predict direct JALs and\\nbackward conditional branches taken, using their encoded PC-relative\\nimmediate, and otherwise predict fall-through. Carry the prediction with\\nthe instruction and have EX redirect and flush only on a misprediction;\\nJALR remains fall-through predicted. Correct loop-back predictions admit\\nthe target instruction into decode instead of paying the current recovery\\nbubble, while avoiding the LUT and timing cost of a BTB or dynamic table.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Decode direct control-flow immediates at fetch, select static BTFNT/JAL next PC, and accept EX recovery only for mispredictions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Extend IF/ID and ID/EX payloads with prediction metadata needed to validate speculative fetch in EX.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Latch IF prediction metadata beside the decoded instruction into ID/EX.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Compare predicted and resolved next PCs, producing a recovery redirect and flush only for control-flow mispredictions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Wire prediction metadata and misprediction recovery through the pipeline and hazard control.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Replace unconditional EX-control-flow flushing with misprediction-only flushing while retaining load and bus-stall priorities.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed BTFNT, direct-JAL, fall-through, and misprediction-recovery tests including RVFI PC sequencing.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r2s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Return-address stack prediction\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 284.75,\n  \"delta_pct\": -8.15,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 120.9,\n  \"cycles\": 4245805,\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Add a compact four-entry return-address stack. Decode pushes PC+4 for\\naccepted link-register calls and pops accepted canonical returns; IF uses\\nthe stack top to predict JALR x0, 0(x1/x5) as a return target. Keep the\\nexisting BTFNT/JAL policy for all other control flow and retain EX's\\npredicted-versus-resolved next-PC comparison as the single recovery path.\\nUpdating only accepted decode instructions prevents wrong-path calls or\\nreturns from corrupting predictor state while removing routine return\\nbubbles from the timed CoreMark call graph.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Accept the RAS top and recognize canonical ABI return JALRs, selecting that target ahead of the sequential fallback.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Classify accepted JAL/JALR link-register calls and canonical returns, then emit compact RAS push/pop update signals only when the instruction is not flushed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add and wire a four-entry return-address stack whose state changes only for accepted decode instructions, preserving the existing nret=1 RVFI contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Continue validating the predicted successor against the resolved JALR target so empty, noncanonical, or stale RAS predictions recover exactly once.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed nested-call, return, empty-stack, and branch-flush-before-call tests, including RVFI PC sequencing through recovery.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Tiny BTFNT-seeded branch direction table\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 193.29,\n  \"delta_pct\": -40.29,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 77.61,\n  \"cycles\": 4015113,\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small direct-mapped, two-bit conditional-branch direction table that\\noverrides BTFNT only after that PC has been observed. On a cold entry, IF\\nkeeps the existing backward-taken/forward-not-taken decision and continues\\nto derive the target solely from the instruction immediate. EX trains the\\ntable with the resolved conditional-branch outcome exactly once when the\\ninstruction advances. This learns stable forward and atypical branch bias\\nwhile preserving the existing narrow fetch target path, direct-JAL policy,\\nrecovery mechanism, and precise behavior under memory stalls.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a small direct-mapped valid-plus-two-bit direction table with combinational PC-indexed lookup, BTFNT-compatible cold entries, and one qualified EX-stage training port.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Use the predictor direction only for validated conditional branches, retaining immediate-only target formation, direct-JAL prediction, and BTFNT fallback on cold table entries.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Emit the resolved conditional-branch PC and architectural direction as a training event only when EX advances, excluding stalled or trapped branch targets.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire the direction predictor between IF and EX without changing the nret=1 top-level or RVFI retirement interface.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed cold-start, saturating-counter, forward-biased, loop-exit, misprediction-recovery, and dmem-stall training tests with RVFI PC-order checks.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Opcode-biased static loop prediction\",\n  \"outcome\": \"improvement\",\n  \"fitness\": 365.65,\n  \"delta_pct\": 1.14,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 147.84,\n  \"cycles\": 4043217,\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Refine the existing stateless BTFNT predictor into an opcode-biased static\\npredictor.  Keep direct JAL prediction unchanged, and predict a backward\\nconditional branch taken only for the loop-continuation predicates\\nBNE, BLT, and BLTU; predict BEQ, BGE, and BGEU fall-through regardless of\\ndisplacement.  The predictor still derives targets solely from the current\\ninstruction immediate and uses the existing EX next-PC comparison for all\\nrecovery, so it adds neither tables nor predictor-state timing while\\navoiding systematic static-direction mistakes on inverted loop exits.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Make static conditional-branch direction depend on funct3 as well as backward displacement, retaining immediate-only target generation and the direct-JAL path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed tests for backward BNE/BLT/BLTU taken predictions and backward BEQ/BGE/BGEU fall-through predictions, including EX recovery and RVFI PC sequencing.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Profiled backward range-loop prediction\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 352.87,\n  \"delta_pct\": -3.5,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 142.13,\n  \"cycles\": 4027817,\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the existing stateless backward-loop predicate to include BGE and\\nBGEU, while retaining fall-through prediction for BEQ and preserving the\\ndirect-JAL path. This is a fetch-local funct3 comparison change: targets are\\nstill formed only from the encoded immediate and EX remains the sole\\narchitectural resolver. It recovers the profiled range-loop back edges\\nwithout adding predictor state, tag RAMs, training logic, or another wide\\nnext-PC mux to the timing-critical fetch path.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Include backward BGE and BGEU in the stateless taken-loop predicate, retaining direct-JAL prediction, immediate-only targets, and BEQ fall-through.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add directed backward BGE and BGEU taken-prediction cases plus loop-exit recovery and RVFI PC-order checks.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Shared static predictor target adder\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 337.65,\n  \"delta_pct\": -7.66,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 136.52,\n  \"cycles\": 4043217,\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Preserve the current direct-JAL and opcode-biased backward BNE/BLT/BLTU\\nprediction policy, but first select a single predicted displacement\\n(four, JAL immediate, or branch immediate) and then compute the successor\\nwith one shared PC adder. This retains identical predicted PCs, EX\\nrecovery, and CoreMark IPC while reducing LUT use and routing pressure in\\nthe timing-sensitive fetch predictor; unlike the failed BHT and RAS, it\\nadds no predictor state, tags, or target mux after a wide arithmetic cone.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Refactor the static JAL and opcode-biased loop predictor to select one immediate displacement before one shared next-PC adder, preserving all existing prediction decisions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add equivalence-oriented predictor tests for direct JAL, backward BNE/BLT/BLTU, fall-through branch classes, redirects, and RVFI PC sequencing.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Minimized static loop predictor\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 284.58,\n  \"delta_pct\": -22.17,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 115.06,\n  \"cycles\": 4043217,\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Preserve exactly the current direct-JAL and backward BNE/BLT/BLTU prediction\\nbehavior, but replace the loop-continuation decode with its minimized Boolean\\nform and remove the redundant reserved-branch validation from that predicate.\\nThe minimized predicate is true only for funct3 values 001, 100, and 110;\\nit therefore cannot predict any reserved branch encoding. This reduces LUT\\ndepth and fanout before the existing parallel target adders and target mux,\\nretaining the proven IPC benefit without adding state or changing recovery.\\n\",\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Replace the equality-chain loop-continuation decode with an exact minimized BNE/BLT/BLTU Boolean predicate while retaining the existing parallel PC-relative adders and prediction semantics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add equivalence-oriented directed cases proving the minimized fetch predicate predicts only backward BNE, BLT, and BLTU, including reserved funct3 fall-through and RVFI PC recovery.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n--- hypothesis schema relevant constraints ---\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n--- target status ---\ndrwxr-xr-x  47 bonetto  staff  1504 Jul 10 23:29 cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
