"improvement\", \"fitness\": 310.0, \"delta_pct\": 9.61, \"vs_baseline\": 9.61, \"fmax_mhz\": 132.05, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4259699, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10490, \"ff\": 1896, \"seeds\": [132.05, 135.98, 130.96], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:03:04.687018Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r1s2 (improvement, +9.61%): Carrying IF's predicted next PC to EX lets a static BTFNT policy avoid recovery bubbles on CoreMark's frequent backward counted-loop branches (and direct JALs), making low-cost fetch-side control prediction an effective IPC optimization without a BTB.\"}\n7:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Return-address stack prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Static BTFNT now predicts CoreMark loop back-edges and direct JAL calls,\\nbut conventional ABI returns still use JALR and therefore default to the\\nfall-through PC. Every frequently called CoreMark helper consequently pays\\nan EX-stage recovery despite its return address being statically available.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Static BTFNT now predicts CoreMark loop back-edges and direct JAL calls,\\nbut conventional ABI returns still use JALR and therefore default to the\\nfall-through PC. Every frequently called CoreMark helper consequently pays\\nan EX-stage recovery despite its return address being statically available.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a compact four-entry return-address stack. Decode pushes PC+4 for\\naccepted link-register calls and pops accepted canonical returns; IF uses\\nthe stack top to predict JALR x0, 0(x1/x5) as a return target. Keep the\\nexisting BTFNT/JAL policy for all other control flow and retain EX's\\npredicted-versus-resolved next-PC comparison as the single recovery path.\\nUpdating only accepted decode instructions prevents wrong-path calls or\\nreturns from corrupting predictor state while removing routine return\\nbubbles from the timed CoreMark call graph.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept the RAS top and recognize canonical ABI return JALRs, selecting that target ahead of the sequential fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify accepted JAL/JALR link-register calls and canonical returns, then emit compact RAS push/pop update signals only when the instruction is not flushed.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Add and wire a four-entry return-address stack whose state changes only for accepted decode instructions, preserving the existing nret=1 RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Continue validating the predicted successor against the resolved JALR target so empty, noncanonical, or stale RAS predictions recover exactly once.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed nested-call, return, empty-stack, and branch-flush-before-call tests, including RVFI PC sequencing through recovery.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept the RAS top and recognize canonical ABI return JALRs, selecting that target ahead of the sequential fallback.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Classify accepted JAL/JALR link-register calls and canonical returns, then emit compact RAS push/pop update signals only when the instruction is not flushed.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Add and wire a four-entry return-address stack whose state changes only for accepted decode instructions, preserving the existing nret=1 RVFI contract.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Continue validating the predicted successor against the resolved JALR target so empty, noncanonical, or stale RAS predictions recover exactly once.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed nested-call, return, empty-stack, and branch-flush-before-call tests, including RVFI PC sequencing through recovery.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 284.75, \"delta_pct\": -8.15, \"vs_baseline\": 0.68, \"fmax_mhz\": 120.9, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4245805, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10868, \"ff\": 2024, \"seeds\": [120.9, 108.24, 125.03], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:17:42.013169Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r2s2 (regression, -8.15%): A RAS-top mux and canonical-return decode on the IF next-PC path can cost more timing than CoreMark gains from avoiding return recoveries, so return prediction must preserve the fetch critical path.\"}\n10:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTFNT-seeded branch direction table\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Static BTFNT already removes the common loop-back recovery bubble, but it\\ncannot learn the bias of forward conditional branches or branches whose\\ndirection differs from their displacement. CoreMark executes such tests in\\nits state machines and list-processing paths. The failed RAS shows that a\\npredictor must not add a wide target mux or substantial decode to fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Static BTFNT already removes the common loop-back recovery bubble, but it\\ncannot learn the bias of forward conditional branches or branches whose\\ndirection differs from their displacement. CoreMark executes such tests in\\nits state machines and list-processing paths. The failed RAS shows that a\\npredictor must not add a wide target mux or substantial decode to fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a small direct-mapped, two-bit conditional-branch direction table that\\noverrides BTFNT only after that PC has been observed. On a cold entry, IF\\nkeeps the existing backward-taken/forward-not-taken decision and continues\\nto derive the target solely from the instruction immediate. EX trains the\\ntable with the resolved conditional-branch outcome exactly once when the\\ninstruction advances. This learns stable forward and atypical branch bias\\nwhile preserving the existing narrow fetch target path, direct-JAL policy,\\nrecovery mechanism, and precise behavior under memory stalls.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small direct-mapped valid-plus-two-bit direction table with combinational PC-indexed lookup, BTFNT-compatible cold entries, and one qualified EX-stage training port.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the predictor direction only for validated conditional branches, retaining immediate-only target formation, direct-JAL prediction, and BTFNT fallback on cold table entries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit the resolved conditional-branch PC and architectural direction as a training event only when EX advances, excluding stalled or trapped branch targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire the direction predictor between IF and EX without changing the nret=1 top-level or RVFI retirement interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed cold-start, saturating-counter, forward-biased, loop-exit, misprediction-recovery, and dmem-stall training tests with RVFI PC-order checks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/branch_predictor.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small direct-mapped valid-plus-two-bit direction table with combinational PC-indexed lookup, BTFNT-compatible cold entries, and one qualified EX-stage training port.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the predictor direction only for validated conditional branches, retaining immediate-only target formation, direct-JAL prediction, and BTFNT fallback on cold table entries.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Emit the resolved conditional-branch PC and architectural direction as a training event only when EX advances, excluding stalled or trapped branch targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Instantiate and wire the direction predictor between IF and EX without changing the nret=1 top-level or RVFI retirement interface.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed cold-start, saturating-counter, forward-biased, loop-exit, misprediction-recovery, and dmem-stall training tests with RVFI PC-order checks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 193.29, \"delta_pct\": -40.29, \"vs_baseline\": -31.66, \"fmax_mhz\": 77.61, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4015113, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10146, \"ff\": 1963, \"seeds\": [81.83, 77.61, 77.21], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:34:05.456895Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3}\n13:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Opcode-biased static loop prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"BTFNT usefully predicts the usual backward counted-loop branch, but it\\ntreats every valid backward conditional branch alike.  CoreMark's loop\\ncontinuations are normally BNE/BLT/BLTU, whereas equality and greater-or-\\nequal branches are often inverted exit or guard tests; predicting those\\nbackward branches taken can introduce repeated recovery bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"BTFNT usefully predicts the usual backward counted-loop branch, but it\\ntreats every valid backward conditional branch alike.  CoreMark's loop\\ncontinuations are normally BNE/BLT/BLTU, whereas equality and greater-or-\\nequal branches are often inverted exit or guard tests; predicting those\\nbackward branches taken can introduce repeated recovery bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Refine the existing stateless BTFNT predictor into an opcode-biased static\\npredictor.  Keep direct JAL prediction unchanged, and predict a backward\\nconditional branch taken only for the loop-continuation predicates\\nBNE, BLT, and BLTU; predict BEQ, BGE, and BGEU fall-through regardless of\\ndisplacement.  The predictor still derives targets solely from the current\\ninstruction immediate and uses the existing EX next-PC comparison for all\\nrecovery, so it adds neither tables nor predictor-state timing while\\navoiding systematic static-direction mistakes on inverted loop exits.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Make static conditional-branch direction depend on funct3 as well as backward displacement, retaining immediate-only target generation and the direct-JAL path.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for backward BNE/BLT/BLTU taken predictions and backward BEQ/BGE/BGEU fall-through predictions, including EX recovery and RVFI PC sequencing.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Make static conditional-branch direction depend on funct3 as well as backward displacement, retaining immediate-only target generation and the direct-JAL path.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed tests for backward BNE/BLT/BLTU taken predictions and backward BEQ/BGE/BGEU fall-through predictions, including EX recovery and RVFI PC sequencing.\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 365.65, \"delta_pct\": 1.14, \"vs_baseline\": 29.29, \"fmax_mhz\": 147.84, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4043217, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9780, \"ff\": 1922, \"seeds\": [147.84, 153.0, 144.99], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:44:50.903850Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r4s2 (improvement, +1.14%): Refining stateless BTFNT to take backward BNE/BLT/BLTU but fall through BEQ/BGE/BGEU better matches CoreMark's counted-loop continuations versus inverted exits, avoiding recurring EX recovery bubbles without adding predictor state or a fetch-path table.\"}\n16:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r5s2\", \"title\": \"Profiled backward range-loop prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current opcode-biased static predictor correctly takes backward BNE, BLT,\\nand BLTU loop continuations, but falls through on every backward BGE and BGEU.\\nA CoreMark retired-instruction profile shows 6,650 backward BGE and 16,320\\nbackward BGEU executions in the timed region, all taken, so these choices\\nstill incur repeated EX recovery bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current opcode-biased static predictor correctly takes backward BNE, BLT,\\nand BLTU loop continuations, but falls through on every backward BGE and BGEU.\\nA CoreMark retired-instruction profile shows 6,650 backward BGE and 16,320\\nbackward BGEU executions in the timed region, all taken, so these choices\\nstill incur repeated EX recovery bubbles.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the existing stateless backward-loop predicate to include BGE and\\nBGEU, while retaining fall-through prediction for BEQ and preserving the\\ndirect-JAL path. This is a fetch-local funct3 comparison change: targets are\\nstill formed only from the encoded immediate and EX remains the sole\\narchitectural resolver. It recovers the profiled range-loop back edges\\nwithout adding predictor state, tag RAMs, training logic, or another wide\\nnext-PC mux to the timing-critical fetch path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Include backward BGE and BGEU in the stateless taken-loop predicate, retaining direct-JAL prediction, immediate-only targets, and BEQ fall-through.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed backward BGE and BGEU taken-prediction cases plus loop-exit recovery and RVFI PC-order checks.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Include backward BGE and BGEU in the stateless taken-loop predicate, retaining direct-JAL prediction, immediate-only targets, and BEQ fall-through.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed backward BGE and BGEU taken-prediction cases plus loop-exit recovery and RVFI PC-order checks.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 352.87, \"delta_pct\": -3.5, \"vs_baseline\": 24.77, \"fmax_mhz\": 142.13, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4027817, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9984, \"ff\": 1918, \"seeds\": [133.99, 142.13, 149.45], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T01:55:31.310215Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r5s2 (regression, -3.50%): In CoreMark, backward BGE/BGEU executions can be biased taken yet still make worse static BTFNT candidates than BNE/BLT/BLTU, so a retired-direction profile alone cannot justify broadening fetch-local loop-continuation funct3 predicates.\"}\n19:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Shared static predictor target adder\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current successful static predictor forms PC+4, PC+JAL-immediate,\\nand PC+branch-immediate in parallel before selecting one result. Those\\nredundant 32-bit adders and their routing sit in the fetch next-PC cone,\\ndespite only one successor ever being required each cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current successful static predictor forms PC+4, PC+JAL-immediate,\\nand PC+branch-immediate in parallel before selecting one result. Those\\nredundant 32-bit adders and their routing sit in the fetch next-PC cone,\\ndespite only one successor ever being required each cycle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Preserve the current direct-JAL and opcode-biased backward BNE/BLT/BLTU\\nprediction policy, but first select a single predicted displacement\\n(four, JAL immediate, or branch immediate) and then compute the successor\\nwith one shared PC adder. This retains identical predicted PCs, EX\\nrecovery, and CoreMark IPC while reducing LUT use and routing pressure in\\nthe timing-sensitive fetch predictor; unlike the failed BHT and RAS, it\\nadds no predictor state, tags, or target mux after a wide arithmetic cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the static JAL and opcode-biased loop predictor to select one immediate displacement before one shared next-PC adder, preserving all existing prediction decisions.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add equivalence-oriented predictor tests for direct JAL, backward BNE/BLT/BLTU, fall-through branch classes, redirects, and RVFI PC sequencing.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Refactor the static JAL and opcode-biased loop predictor to select one immediate displacement before one shared next-PC adder, preserving all existing prediction decisions.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add equivalence-oriented predictor tests for direct JAL, backward BNE/BLT/BLTU, fall-through branch classes, redirects, and RVFI PC sequencing.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 337.65, \"delta_pct\": -7.66, \"vs_baseline\": 19.39, \"fmax_mhz\": 136.52, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4043217, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10205, \"ff\": 1922, \"seeds\": [142.94, 136.52, 136.44], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:11:33.325304Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r6s2 (regression, -7.66%): On the fetch-critical Tang Nano predictor path, selecting a 32-bit JAL/branch/sequential displacement before a shared PC adder puts a wide target mux ahead of carry propagation, so parallel PC-relative adders followed by target selection can place and time better despite redundant arithmetic.\"}\n22:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Minimized static loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The best CoreMark result uses a stateless fetch-local policy, but its\\nBNE/BLT/BLTU selector is currently expressed as several three-bit equality\\ncomparisons plus a redundant branch-validity check in the next-PC cone.\\nThis cone is timing-sensitive on the Tang Nano 20K.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The best CoreMark result uses a stateless fetch-local policy, but its\\nBNE/BLT/BLTU selector is currently expressed as several three-bit equality\\ncomparisons plus a redundant branch-validity check in the next-PC cone.\\nThis cone is timing-sensitive on the Tang Nano 20K.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Preserve exactly the current direct-JAL and backward BNE/BLT/BLTU prediction\\nbehavior, but replace the loop-continuation decode with its minimized Boolean\\nform and remove the redundant reserved-branch validation from that predicate.\\nThe minimized predicate is true only for funct3 values 001, 100, and 110;\\nit therefore cannot predict any reserved branch encoding. This reduces LUT\\ndepth and fanout before the existing parallel target adders and target mux,\\nretaining the proven IPC benefit without adding state or changing recovery.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the equality-chain loop-continuation decode with an exact minimized BNE/BLT/BLTU Boolean predicate while retaining the existing parallel PC-relative adders and prediction semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add equivalence-oriented directed cases proving the minimized fetch predicate predicts only backward BNE, BLT, and BLTU, including reserved funct3 fall-through and RVFI PC recovery.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Replace the equality-chain loop-continuation decode with an exact minimized BNE/BLT/BLTU Boolean predicate while retaining the existing parallel PC-relative adders and prediction semantics.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add equivalence-oriented directed cases proving the minimized fetch predicate predicts only backward BNE, BLT, and BLTU, including reserved funct3 fall-through and RVFI PC recovery.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 284.58, \"delta_pct\": -22.17, \"vs_baseline\": 0.62, \"fmax_mhz\": 115.06, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4043217, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10028, \"ff\": 1922, \"seeds\": [115.06, 122.53, 112.08], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:24:09.769271Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r7s2 (regression, -22.17%): On the fetch-critical Tang Nano next-PC cone, hand-minimizing the BNE/BLT/BLTU funct3 predicate can map and place worse than direct equality decodes despite identical branch behavior, so Boolean gate-count reduction alone is not a reliable timing optimization.\"}\n25:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260710-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"Decode-stage branch correction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The opcode-biased static predictor removes most loop back-edge bubbles, but\\nits intentional fall-through choices and final loop exits still recover only\\nafter EX. CoreMark executes many such conditional branches, so moving safe\\nmisprediction correction one stage earlier can raise IPC without a fetch\\ntable, RAS, or extra next-PC target-selection cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The opcode-biased static predictor removes most loop back-edge bubbles, but\\nits intentional fall-through choices and final loop exits still recover only\\nafter EX. CoreMark executes many such conditional branches, so moving safe\\nmisprediction correction one stage earlier can raise IPC without a fetch\\ntable, RAS, or extra next-PC target-selection cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a source-ready decode-stage branch resolver that validates only\\nconditional-branch predictions. When neither branch source is pending from\\nan older EX or MEM producer, ID compares the write-first regfile operands,\\nforms the existing PC-relative target, and redirects IF immediately on a\\npredicted-versus-actual mismatch. Carry the corrected successor as the\\nbranch's prediction so EX does not redirect a second time. If either source\\nis pending, a memory hold is active, or the branch target is misaligned, ID\\ndefers unchanged to the existing EX resolver. This retains the proven\\nstateless fetch policy and precise RVFI behavior while reducing the recovery\\npenalty of independent branch misses by one cycle.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-ready conditional-branch comparison, immediate target generation, and an early correction signal while preserving the normal ID/EX payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect older branch-source producers, arbitrate EX recovery over ID correction, and pass the corrected predicted successor into the pipeline without changing the top-level IO.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Handle an ID-only correction by flushing the fetched slot while allowing the correcting branch to advance, with EX recovery and dmem-hold priority retained.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept the arbitrated earlier correction through the existing redirect-over-stall PC update path and emit the required speculative-fetch bubble.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Continue exact branch resolution and use the corrected ID successor as prediction metadata, preserving the EX fallback for dependencies and traps.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add independent branch-miss, ALU/load-dependent fallback, dmem-stalled, simultaneous EX-redirect, and RVFI PC/order directed tests.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add source-ready conditional-branch comparison, immediate target generation, and an early correction signal while preserving the normal ID/EX payload.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Detect older branch-source producers, arbitrate EX recovery over ID correction, and pass the corrected predicted successor into the pipeline without changing the top-level IO.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Handle an ID-only correction by flushing the fetched slot while allowing the correcting branch to advance, with EX recovery and dmem-hold priority retained.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Accept the arbitrated earlier correction through the existing redirect-over-stall PC update path and emit the required speculative-fetch bubble.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Continue exact branch resolution and use the corrected ID successor as prediction metadata, preserving the EX fallback for dependencies and traps.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Add independent branch-miss, ALU/load-dependent fallback, dmem-stalled, simultaneous EX-redirect, and RVFI PC/order directed tests.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 287.28, \"delta_pct\": -21.43, \"vs_baseline\": 1.58, \"fmax_mhz\": 115.05, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4004858, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10478, \"ff\": 1902, \"seeds\": [112.68, 115.05, 117.65], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T02:44:00.400249Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-10 hyp-20260710-003-r8s2 (regression, -21.43%): Resolving source-ready conditional branches in ID puts two-source comparison, EX/MEM producer-scoreboarding, PC-target generation, and the ID-to-IF redirect mux on the front-end critical path, costing more timing than CoreMark recovers from a one-cycle-earlier misprediction fix.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
