{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The strongest remaining evidence points to the same registered-control-to-EX cone: the current partition still routes the ADD-class suboperation bit through the ALU result path. I’m narrowing that further by making subtraction its own result class, leaving common ADD/address generation without a second-level suboperation mux."}}
