{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; d = YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r10s0.yaml\\\"); abort(\\\"bad id\\\") unless d[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20260711-001-r10s0\\\"; abort(\\\"bad category\\\") unless d[\\\"category\\\"] == \\\"micro_opt\\\"; abort(\\\"bad impact\\\") unless d.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\").is_a?(Integer) && d.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"confidence\\\") == \\\"medium\\\"; abort(\\\"bad paths\\\") unless d.fetch(\\\"changes\\\").all? { |c| c.fetch(\\\"file\\\").match?(%r{\\\\A(?:rtl/|test/test_).+}) }; puts \\\"YAML structure OK\\\"' && git diff --check && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r10s0.yaml && sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r10s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"YAML structure OK\nid: hyp-20260711-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Promote SUB to ALU result class\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The latest class-partitioned ALU raised Fmax substantially, but the common\n  ADD class still selects ADD versus SUB through a second-level suboperation\n  control. Route reports before that partition identified this registered ALU\n  control cone as timing-sensitive, while CoreMark is dominated by ADDI,\n  address generation, and AUIPC rather than subtraction.\nhypothesis: |\n  Encode SUB as its own base result class and reserve the class-local\n  suboperation field for logic, compare, and shift operations. The ADD class\n  will then drive its adder directly, with no ADD/SUB selection below the\n  result-class split; loads, stores, ADD/ADDI, and AUIPC retain exactly the\n  same single-cycle arithmetic and forwarding behavior. This is a focused\n  continuation of the proven ALU mux partitioning, intended to shorten the\n  remaining control-to-adder path without changing pipeline depth, prediction,\n  or RV32IM semantics.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a dedicated SUB base-result class and redefine the base local suboperation field as unused for ADD and SUB.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Emit the SUB class only for validated SUB encodings while leaving ADD, ADDI, loads, stores, and AUIPC in the direct ADD class.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Carry the revised base result-class control through ID/EX without changing operand capture, valid, stall, or flush behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Connect the unchanged-width refined ALU control to execute while preserving forwarding, branch resolution, and EX/MEM timing.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Make ADD and SUB separate first-level base result branches so the ADD output has no nested ADD/SUB suboperation mux; retain all other base and M results.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Add directed ADD/SUB class-boundary vectors plus regression coverage for address generation, logic, compare, shift, LUI, and RV32M operations.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
