and validation loops use equality as their continuing\\npredicate, so each taken backward BEQ still pays an EX recovery bubble.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Extend the existing direct-JAL plus opcode-biased backward-branch predictor\\nto predict valid backward BEQ instructions taken as well. Retain the\\nparallel PC+4, JAL-target, and branch-target adders and the existing EX\\npredicted-versus-resolved recovery path. This is a single fetch-local\\npredicate expansion with no predictor state, tags, training, or new target\\nmuxing, so it can recover equality-loop bubbles while preserving the\\ntiming-friendly implementation that rejected dynamic predictor attempts.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Include backward BEQ in the existing valid static loop-continuation predicate while retaining direct-JAL prediction, parallel target generation, and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed backward-BEQ taken-prediction and not-taken recovery cases, including reserved BRANCH encodings that must remain fall-through predicted.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 2, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Include backward BEQ in the existing valid static loop-continuation predicate while retaining direct-JAL prediction, parallel target generation, and redirect priority.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed backward-BEQ taken-prediction and not-taken recovery cases, including reserved BRANCH encodings that must remain fall-through predicted.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 342.87, \"delta_pct\": -33.51, \"vs_baseline\": 21.23, \"fmax_mhz\": 139.61, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4071751, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10249, \"ff\": 1922, \"seeds\": [139.37, 139.61, 174.43], \"formal_passed\": true,