\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r4s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r4s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r5s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r6s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r6s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r7s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r7s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r8s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r8s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r9s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260710-003-r9s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r10s0.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r10s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r11s0.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r11s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r12s0.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r12s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r13s0.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r10s1.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r10s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r11s1.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r11s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r12s1.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r12s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-002-r13s1.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r10s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r11s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r11s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r12s2.last\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r12s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-003-r13s2.log\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r13s1.yaml\\ncores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-003-r13s2.yaml\\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\ncores/bench/experiments/progress.png\\ncores/bench/experiments/run_summary.json\\n\",\"exit_code\":1,\"status\":\"failed\"}}\n\n--- last ---\nsed: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260711-001-r13s0.last: No such file or directory\n\n--- peer YAML ---\nid: hyp-20260711-002-r13s1\ntitle: \"Restartable iterative RV32M divider\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current ALU elaborates four real combinational divide/remainder expressions,\n  which are high-fanout LUT-heavy cones even though CoreMark's hot loop is mostly\n  integer arithmetic, pointer loads, stores, and branches. Earlier frontend and\n  store-buffer structures either hurt placement or added timing-critical control.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace only DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU with a single 32-step restoring divider\n  that owns one held EX instruction until a result is ready; all other ALU and\n  multiply operations retain the existing one-cycle EX path. Dispatch must be\n  edge-qualified so a held divide starts once, and completion injects precisely\n  one normal EX/MEM record. Keep the existing RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS expressions\n  for formal builds, and implement divide-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 cases directly\n  in the sequencer. Removing the four combinational arithmetic cones should free\n  LUT/routing pressure and raise Fmax, while any multi-cycle cost is limited to\n  comparatively infrequent divide instructions.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Keep base and multiply operations combinational, retain ALTOPS behavior, and remove real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU operators from the normal EX result cone.\"\n  - file: rtl/divider_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add one restart-safe unsigned restoring divider with signed operand/result correction, operation selection, busy/done handshake, and all RV32M exceptional results.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Dispatch divide/remainder operations once, hold their complete decoded payload while the divider is busy, and emit one EX/MEM result only on completion.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add execute-busy pipeline interlocking that preserves older MEM progress, freezes younger work, and maintains redirect priority without duplicate retirement.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire divider request, busy, completion, and result signals through the existing single-issue pipeline without changing the nret=1 IO or RVFI boundary.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Exercise all DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU signedness and corner cases through the iterative result path.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add divide launch-once, dependent consumer, imem/dmem-stall, RVFI-order, and forward-progress tests for the multi-cycle EX hold.\"\nid: hyp-20260711-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Lean static loop predictor predecode\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current direct-JAL plus backward BNE/BLT/BLTU policy is the only\n  predictor policy that has consistently improved CoreMark IPC. Its fetch\n  classifier also computes a branch-legality predicate that is redundant\n  when the selected loop-continuation funct3 values are already all legal.\nhypothesis: |\n  Preserve the exact static predictions for direct JAL and backward\n  BNE/BLT/BLTU, but collapse the fetch-side branch qualification to the\n  selected funct3 tests themselves. Remove the separate valid-branch decode\n  and keep the existing parallel PC+4, JAL-target, and branch-target paths.\n  This leaves architectural behavior and prediction accuracy unchanged while\n  reducing control fanout and logic on the fetch-critical next-PC selection.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Remove the redundant branch-legality qualification from the BNE/BLT/BLTU static predictor while retaining its exact prediction behavior, direct-JAL path, parallel target generation, and redirect priority.\"\n  - file: test/test_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add equivalence-oriented directed checks for backward BNE, BLT, and BLTU predictions, fall-through behavior for other branch funct3 values, and correct recovery under instruction-memory stalls.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
