{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --check && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r14s0.yaml && ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; require \\\"json\\\"; h=YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-001-r14s0.yaml\\\"); s=JSON.parse(File.read(\\\"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json\\\")); abort \\\"id\\\" unless h[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20260711-001-r14s0\\\"; abort \\\"category\\\" unless h[\\\"category\\\"] == \\\"micro_opt\\\"; abort \\\"impact\\\" unless h[\\\"expected_impact\\\"][\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\"].is_a?(Integer) && %w[low medium high].include?(h[\\\"expected_impact\\\"][\\\"confidence\\\"]); abort \\\"paths\\\" unless h[\\\"changes\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(%r{\\\\A(?:rtl/[\"'^.].*|test/test_[''^/]+'\"\\\\.py)\\\\z}) }; puts \\\"YAML shape checks passed\\\"' && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20260711-001-r14s0\ntitle: \"Registered retirement trace boundary\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The FPGA wrapper deliberately retains every RVFI field by XOR-reducing\n  them into the LED. Today those wide outputs are driven combinationally\n  from MEM/WB, including the writeback mux and RVFI qualification logic.\n  That creates a broad physical fanout from the retirement cone even though\n  tracing is not needed to execute the next instruction.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add one dedicated RVFI trace register at the existing retirement boundary.\n  Capture every RVFI field and the pre-increment retirement order from the\n  current valid MEM/WB instruction, then drive the required top-level RVFI\n  ports solely from that register on the following cycle. Keep register-file\n  writeback, memory completion, marker timing, and all pipeline forwarding\n  on their present paths; the added state is observability-only. This cuts\n  the wide MEM/WB-to-port/LED combinational fanout while preserving one\n  ordered retirement record per completed instruction and its exact operand,\n  result, PC, trap, and memory fields.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Add a packed or fieldwise RVFI trace register that captures the current MEM/WB retirement record and pre-increment order, drives every channel-0 RVFI output from the registered record, and preserves the nret=1 IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add retirement-trace latency coverage for ALU, load, store, illegal, and dmem-stalled instructions, checking exact RVFI fields, monotonic order, and exactly one valid trace record per execution retirement.\"\nYAML shape checks passed\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
