07/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-002-r14s1 (broken, n/a): Retiming operand capture into a separate EX1 stage requires every RAW forwarding source, especially the late MEM-load result, to supply the final value at the new boundary; otherwise dependent instructions capture stale operands and violate riscv-formal's register check.\"}\ncores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:43:{\"id\": \"hyp-20260711-003-r14s2\", \"title\": \"Certify direct JAL prediction\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Direct JALs are already predicted taken in IF from their encoded PC-relative\\nimmediate. For an aligned target that prediction is exact, yet EX still\\nforms and compares two 32-bit successor values before deciding not to\\nredirect. This redundant recovery check remains in the control-flow cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Direct JALs are already predicted taken in IF from their encoded PC-relative\\nimmediate. For an aligned target that prediction is exact, yet EX still\\nforms and compares two 32-bit successor values before deciding not to\\nredirect. This redundant recovery check remains in the control-flow cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Treat an aligned direct JAL as a certified static prediction: preserve its\\nexisting IF target calculation and normal EX PC-next/RVFI result, but bypass\\nEX's predicted-versus-resolved 32-bit equality test for that instruction.\\nConditional branches and JALR retain the current comparison and recovery,\\nwhile a misaligned JAL still traps and redirects to the sequential PC. This\\nkeeps the proven direct-JAL/BNE/BLT/BLTU policy and IPC unchanged while\\nremoving a redundant wide compare and its redirect-control fanout from the\\ncommon direct-call execution path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress redirect comparison for valid aligned direct JALs, while retaining resolved PC-next, misalignment trapping, and existing branch/JALR recovery behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed direct-JAL certification tests covering aligned targets, misaligned-target trap recovery, bus stalls, and exact RVFI PC sequencing.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Suppress redirect comparison for valid aligned direct JALs, while retaining resolved PC-next, misalignment trapping, and existing branch/JALR recovery behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_predictor.py\", \"description\": \"Add directed direct-JAL certification tests covering aligned targets, misaligned-target trap recovery, bus stalls, and exact RVFI PC sequencing.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 477.84, \"delta_pct\": -7.34, \"vs_baseline\": 68.96, \"fmax_mhz\": 193.2, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4043217, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 10538, \"ff\": 1922, \"seeds\": [188.22, 195.27, 193.2], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-11T04:12:20.226461Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-07-11 hyp-20260711-003-r14s2 (regression, -7.34%): Bypassing the EX successor equality check for statically exact direct JALs can still regress on Tang Nano because the JAL-certification decode, alignment qualification, and redirect-select mux add control delay and fanout to the shared redirect cone, outweighing removal of a well-mapped 32-bit compare.\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
