{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; require \\\"json\\\"; h=YAML.load_file(ARGV[0]); s=JSON.parse(File.read(ARGV[1])); abort \\\"id\\\" unless h[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20260711-002-r10s1\\\"; abort \\\"category\\\" unless h[\\\"category\\\"] == \\\"structural\\\"; abort \\\"impact\\\" unless h.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\").is_a?(Integer) && %w[low medium high].include?(h.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"confidence\\\")); abort \\\"changes\\\" unless h[\\\"changes\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(%r{\\\\A(?:rtl/[\"'^.].*|test/test_[''^/]+'\"\\\\.py)\\\\z}) }; puts \\\"YAML structure checks passed\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r10s1.yaml schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && git diff --check && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r10s1.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r10s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"YAML structure checks passed\nid: hyp-20260711-002-r10s1\ntitle: \"Tiny direct-mapped instruction cache\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The performance cosimulation injects independent instruction-bus stalls on\n  every fetched word, while CoreMark repeatedly executes a compact set of hot\n  loop bodies. The current combinational fetch path must wait for each such\n  bus acceptance, and prior queue designs added enough wide control and data\n  routing to lose far more Fmax than their overlap recovered.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a small, one-word-line direct-mapped instruction cache between IF and\n  the existing instruction-memory port. Each cache line holds a valid bit,\n  word address tag, and instruction; a hit supplies the current PC's word\n  without requiring io_imemReady, while a miss retains the existing request\n  and fill-on-accepted-response behavior. Keep the present static JAL and\n  backward-loop prediction unchanged and invalidate only speculative cache\n  control state on reset, not cached instructions on redirects. This is a\n  bounded structural source of stall tolerance that avoids a FIFO's\n  enqueue/dequeue paths and should capture CoreMark's repeatedly fetched hot\n  instructions after warm-up.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/icache.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact direct-mapped, one-word-line instruction cache with tag, valid, accepted-fill, hit, and miss-request interfaces.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use cache hits as valid fetch responses, hold a miss PC until its bus response is accepted, and preserve the existing fetch-local prediction and redirect priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate and wire the instruction cache between the unchanged imem ports and IF, exposing cache miss state to pipeline control without altering the core IO or RVFI boundary.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Replace raw imem-ready flushing with a qualified cache-miss wait so cache hits continue to issue during external instruction-bus stalls.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add cache cold-miss, hit-under-imem-stall, refill, redirect, and mixed dmem-stall tests checking in-order RVFI PCs, orders, and no duplicate fetch retirement.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
