{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ruby -e 'require \\\"yaml\\\"; require \\\"json\\\"; h=YAML.load_file(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r11s1.yaml\\\"); abort(\\\"bad id\\\") unless h[\\\"id\\\"] == \\\"hyp-20260711-002-r11s1\\\"; abort(\\\"bad category\\\") unless h[\\\"category\\\"] == \\\"structural\\\"; abort(\\\"bad impact\\\") unless h.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\").is_a?(Integer) && %w[low medium high].include?(h.dig(\\\"expected_impact\\\", \\\"confidence\\\")); abort(\\\"bad files\\\") unless h[\\\"changes\\\"].all? { |c| c[\\\"file\\\"].match?(%r{\\\\A(?:rtl/[\"'^.].*|test/test_[''^/]+'\"\\\\.py)\\\\z}) }; puts \\\"hypothesis YAML valid: #{h[\\\"changes\\\"].length} changes\\\"' && git status --short -- cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r11s1.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260711-002-r11s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"hypothesis YAML valid: 8 changes\nid: hyp-20260711-002-r11s1\ntitle: \"MEM-stage completion and retirement\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The existing MEM/WB record transports a full RVFI snapshot through an\n  additional pipeline register after all architectural memory work has\n  completed. This wide record and its writeback/RVFI fanout consume routing\n  near a design already above the LUT target, without improving steady-state\n  issue bandwidth.\nhypothesis: |\n  Collapse the MEM/WB stage into an acknowledged MEM completion boundary.\n  Retire and write the register file directly from the EX/MEM instruction\n  once a load or store is accepted (or immediately for a non-memory op), and\n  construct RVFI from that same completion snapshot. Keep only a narrow\n  registered writeback-bypass record for the one older producer needed by\n  EX forwarding. This removes the wide MEM/WB state and its broad routing\n  while keeping the zero-bubble load bypass, in-order retirement, and the\n  existing stall behavior; it should improve placement/Fmax without adding\n  fetch-path logic or an IPC penalty.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Replace the full MEM/WB payload with a compact writeback-bypass record and define the MEM completion fields needed for direct RVFI construction.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose an accepted completion snapshot, including qualified load data, aligned memory observations, trap qualification, and a retire-valid signal that is suppressed while an active memory request is unacknowledged.\"\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: \"Select direct MEM-completion writeback data and maintain only the narrow registered producer result required for the older EX forwarding case.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Retarget the older-producer forwarding input from the removed MEM/WB record to the compact writeback-bypass record, retaining youngest-producer priority and the load bypass.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume the revised compact older-writeback forwarding source without changing EX/MEM execution, branch resolution, or same-cycle load forwarding.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Qualify memory completion and pipeline holds so dmem backpressure cannot cause a direct-MEM retirement or register write to repeat.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Move channel-0 RVFI, rvfi_order advancement, and regfile write enable to the MEM completion boundary while preserving the nret=1 top-level port contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Add ALU/load/store completion-boundary tests under random imem/dmem stalls, checking exact RVFI fields, strict order, writeback forwarding, and one retirement per accepted instruction.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
