the proven\\nfetch or EX critical cones.\\n\",\n  \"expected_impact\": {\n    \"fitness_delta_pct\": 5,\n    \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/store_queue.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Add a one-entry posted RAM-store latch holding aligned address, replicated data, byte mask, valid state, and same-edge drain/refill control.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Classify qualified aligned stores as RAM versus MMIO, enqueue eligible RAM writes as MEM completions, and block loads/MMIO until an older queued store drains.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Replace store-only whole-pipeline dmem holds with queue-full and load/MMIO ordering holds while retaining response-qualified load stalls and redirect priority.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Arbitrate the unchanged dmem port between queued writes and the active MEM instruction, and preserve single-channel RVFI retirement and order semantics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Add randomized stalled RAM-store streams, drain/refill, store-to-load fencing, partial writes, UART and timing-marker ordering, and strict RVFI-order checks.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
