d address, so the\\nload-use interlock no longer injects its otherwise mandatory bubble. Keep\\nthe pair frozen under dmem backpressure and suppress the bypass for\\nmisaligned trapping accesses; therefore retirement order, RVFI operand\\nvalues, and all existing exception behavior remain unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the existing extracted load result plus a valid signal qualified by a real, aligned accepted load for same-cycle bypassing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Distinguish an EX/MEM load from an ALU producer and select the dedicated MEM-load forwarding source for matching EX operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the MEM-load forwarding input and select it for either source operand while retaining ALU and WB forwarding priority rules.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the proactive load-use bubble; retain the full-pipeline hold for an unaccepted dmem transaction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the qualified load-result bypass from MEM to execute and the revised forwarding controls without changing core IO or RVFI retirement.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Replace the one-bubble load-use expectation with directed zero-wait and dmem-stalled dependency tests that check data, RVFI order, and single retirement.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Expose the existing extracted load result plus a valid signal qualified by a real, aligned accepted load for same-cycle bypassing.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Distinguish an EX/MEM load from an ALU producer and select the dedicated MEM-load forwarding source for matching EX operands.\"}, {\"file\": \"rt